    "basis": "35 mm bar tile with three added countertop dish groups and two hidden plate stacks plus goblet. Independent 72000/24000 triangle meshes and 1024/512 bakes preserve ceramic lips, open rear shelving, carved timber and fasteners. Compare compact 768/384 maps."
  },
  "reviewNotes": "PDF page 8 and native source front/back/top inspected. Source has 399952 triangles, 19997684 bytes and height 48.341797 mm. Full-height centre ray reaches floor at 24.706406 mm, normal Z=.98321; 17 mm mount datum. Floor normal squares X=.375895, Y=.040710 confirm Y grain. Countertop has one shallow south bowl (Z<=45.4325), a central plate stack (Z<=47.6001), and a north bowl stack (Z<=48.3418). Three groups were separated above 43.55 mm; measured XY bounds are recorded in their masks. Common countertop timber compared with MT1-044: 435 probes, median .001882 mm, P95 .011666 mm, max .027367 mm. The .08 mm reference threshold separates added ceramic from shared timber; projecting packed geometry to MT1-045 prevents simplification from painting wood. Three exposed fasteners were measured; the fourth is covered by the south bowl. Internal shelf ceramics retain independently bounded masks from the common sculpt. Review both sides, top, ceramic/wood contacts, source bowl depths, both LOD tiers and texture candidates.",
